    "updated_at": "2017-10-12T22:12:01Z",
    "body": "@sudsj, there are two parts to this:\r\n 1. Changing what the spec says to not have this bug.\r\n 2. Writing tests that show that this bug doesn't exist in implementations.\r\n\r\nI think starting with the tests may be most productive, since if it turns out that some or all browsers do have this bug, we may need to think harder about how to fix it. Add a test in https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/tree/master/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/loading-the-media-resource that would fall into this case, and see if the load event really is delayed indefinitely.\r\n\r\nTo trigger this case in the first place, you need to trigger the resource selection algorithm, and then undo the thing that triggered it, for example by adding and removing a `<source>` child element.\r\n\r\nSee http://web-platform-tests.org/writing-tests/ for general guidance on writing tests.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
